e of contents","f":[]},{"s":33729,"e":33807,"k":"block","t":"\n      KTPH000KTPH001\n      Table of contents\n    ","f":["<span class=\"md-nav__icon md-icon\">","</span>"]},{"s":33928,"e":34059,"k":"block","t":"\n  KTPH000\n    KTPH001\n      \n        Dashboard\n      \n    KTPH002\n  KTPH003\n  \n","f":["<a href=\"#dashboard\" class=\"md-nav__link\">","<span class=\"md-ellipsis\">","</span>","</a>"]},{"s":34105,"e":34248,"k":"block","t":"\n  KTPH000\n    KTPH001\n      \n        macOS Dock menu\n      \n    KTPH002\n  KTPH003\n  \n","f":["<a href=\"#macos-dock-menu\" class=\"md-nav__link\">","<span class=\"md-ellipsis\">","</span>","</a>"]},{"s":34595,"e":34699,"k":"block","t":"Main window overviewKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#main-window-overview\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":34708,"e":34789,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"korTTY main window\" src=\"../assets/screenshots/main/main-window.png\" />"]},{"s":34797,"e":34876,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Main window layout\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/mainwindow-layout.svg\" />"]},{"s":34884,"e":35076,"k":"block","t":"A fresh korTTY window: the menu bar, the terminal area (where session tabs and the optional dashboard appear once you connect), and the status bar. The following diagram maps the same regions:","f":[]},{"s":35084,"e":35159,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"korTTY architecture\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/architecture.svg\" />"]},{"s":35167,"e":35206,"k":"block","t":"korTTY's main window has these regions:","f":[]},{"s":35220,"e":35825,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Menu barKTPH001 — File · Edit · Connections · Security · Configuration · Tools · Plugins · View · Teamwork · AI · Help. All features are reachable here and via KTPH002keyboard shortcutsKTPH003. A live KTPH004JobScheduler statusKTPH005 menu appears after KTPH006HelpKTPH007 when a scheduled entry is active. While a KTPH008guide translationKTPH009 runs, a progress indicator (bar, percentage and estimated time remaining) sits at the right end of the menu-bar row and stays visible even when the menu bar itself is hidden.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>","<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>","<a href=\"../reference/settings/translation.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":35835,"e":36601,"k":"block","t":"KTPH007Tab barKTPH008 — each SSH/Mosh session runs in its own tab. KTPH009KTPH000KTPH010+KTPH011KTPH001KTPH012 opens Quick Connect for a new tab; KTPH013KTPH002KTPH014+KTPH015KTPH003KTPH016 / KTPH017KTPH004KTPH018+KTPH019KTPH005KTPH020+KTPH021KTPH006KTPH022 switch tabs. With KTPH023Open tool windows as tabsKTPH024 enabled (KTPH025Window settingsKTPH026), management tools such as Snippets, the JobScheduler or the AI Manager open here as tabs too — in the window whose menu you used — instead of as separate windows.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-t\">T</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/settings/window.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":36611,"e":36942,"k":"block","t":"KTPH003DashboardKTPH004 (toggle KTPH005KTPH000KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH001KTPH008+KTPH009KTPH002KTPH010) — a side panel listing every open connection with status dots, protocol badges and AI-agent badges. See KTPH011DashboardKTPH012 below.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<a href=\"#dashboard\">","</a>"]},{"s":36952,"e":37323,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000File browserKTPH001 (KTPH002View → File Browser ▸ Show on Left / Show on RightKTPH003) — a dockable local file manager with navigation toolbar, path bar, filter, type icons and a folder/file/selection counter. Its side, width, hidden-file state and last directory are restored on the next launch. See KTPH004File browserKTPH005.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../features/file-browser.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":37333,"e":37775,"k":"block","t":"KTPH003Live journal panelKTPH004 (KTPH005View → Live JournalKTPH006, KTPH007KTPH000KTPH008+KTPH009KTPH001KTPH010+KTPH011KTPH002KTPH012) — the active tab's running KTPH013session journalKTPH014 as its full journal page, docked and updating in real time; side and width are restored on the next launch.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-alt\">Alt</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-l\">L</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<a href=\"../features/session-journal.html#the-live-journal-panel\">","</a>"]},{"s":37785,"e":37886,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Terminal areaKTPH001 — the active terminal, with optional split-screen and broadcast input.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37896,"e":38018,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Status barKTPH001 — connection state, host/IP, active protocol, temporary SSH-key timer and connection duration.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38087,"e":38111,"k":"block","t":"Terminal-only fullscreen","f":[]},{"s":38119,"e":38932,"k":"block","t":"Press KTPH006KTPH000KTPH007+KTPH008KTPH001KTPH009+KTPH010KTPH002KTPH011 (or KTPH012View → Terminal-only FullscreenKTPH013) to show the whole korTTY window — menus, tabs and status bar included — kept at its previous window size and centered on an empty fullscreen background, so the desktop and other windows stop competing for attention. KTPH014View → Hide terminal scrollbars in fullscreenKTPH015 removes the scrollbars too. A transparent terminal background becomes opaque while fullscreen is active and returns to its saved level when you leave. Press KTPH016KTPH003KTPH017+KTPH018KTPH004KTPH019+KTPH020KTPH005KTPH021 again to restore.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>"]},{"s":38963,"e":39045,"k":"block","t":"DashboardKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#dashboard\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":39054,"e":39380,"k":"block","t":"Toggle the dashboard with KTPH003KTPH000KTPH004+KTPH005KTPH001KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH002KTPH008 or KTPH009View → Show DashboardKTPH010. It slides in on the left, sizes its width to the longest entry, and follows the active App Design's colors.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39388,"e":39608,"k":"block","t":"The header shows the panel title with two buttons: a collapse/expand toggle (collapses everything while any node is open, expands everything otherwise) and a refresh button. Below it, connections are organized as a tree:","f":[]},{"s":39622,"e":39703,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Main windowKTPH001 — the root node, with an active/total session count.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39713,"e":39951,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000EnvironmentsKTPH001 — connections whose stored credential has an environment (for example KTPH002ProductionKTPH003 or KTPH004TestKTPH005) are clustered under an environment node; connections without one sit directly under the main window.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":39961,"e":40133,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000GroupsKTPH001 — tabs assigned to a connection group appear under their group node. Saving a changed group in the Connection Manager updates open tabs immediately.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":40148,"e":40780,"k":"block","t":"Each connection row shows a type icon, a status dot, the server name, and a protocol badge (KTPH000, KTPH001 or KTPH002). The status dot distinguishes three states: filled green for a healthy connection, filled red for a connection that dropped unexpectedly (including a Mosh network interruption), and a hollow outline for a session that ended normally. Terminals with AI-agent runs carry the same ✋/⚡/⏸/✓ badge as elsewhere. Hovering a row shows KTPH003 and the connection state; double-click (or KTPH005KTPH004KTPH006) focuses the session's tab.","f":["<code>ssh</code>","<code>mosh</code>","<code>local</code>","<code>user@host</code>","<kbd class=\"key-enter\">Enter</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","</span>"]},{"s":40788,"e":41105,"k":"block","t":"Right-click a connection for KTPH000FocusKTPH001, KTPH002DuplicateKTPH003, KTPH004ReconnectKTPH005, KTPH006SFTP-Client...KTPH007 (connected sessions only) and KTPH008CloseKTPH009. A footer keeps a running \"connected of total\" count, and an empty panel shows a placeholder until the first session opens.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41135,"e":41229,"k":"block","t":"macOS Dock menuKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#macos-dock-menu\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":41238,"e":41434,"k":"block","t":"On macOS, right-click (or Control-click) the korTTY icon in the Dock for quick actions without switching to the app — they apply to the current (focused) window, opening one first if none is open:","f":[]},{"s":41448,"e":41475,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41485,"e":41527,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New Tab in Current WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41537,"e":41594,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Manage Connections…KTPH001 (Connection Manager)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41604,"e":41634,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Open Project…KTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41644,"e":41686,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000ManualKTPH001 (the in-app guide)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41696,"e":41725,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000About korTTYKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41740,"e":41942,"k":"block","t":"See the KTPH000menu referenceKTPH001 for every menu item and the KTPH002keyboard-shortcuts referenceKTPH003 for the full list of accelerators.","f":["<a href=\"../reference/menu.html\">","</a>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":42813,"e":42828,"k":"text","t":"\n  Back to top\n","f":[]},{"s":43071,"e":43112,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":43158,"e":43170,"k":"text","t":"\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":43178,"e":43185,"k":"text","t":"v2.11.0","f":[]}]}